      "writtenOn": "2024-09-20T15:05:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any reason to prefer that approach over committing to `SkPathBuilder` and making `SkPath` const?\n\nIn its current form, `SkPath` is mutable AND a poor path builder (non-trivial editor dance, non-reusable buffer allocations, complex state tracking using atomics, etc).  OTOH I can\u0027t think of anything wrong with `SkPathBuilder` that would justify throwing it away and converting `SkPath` into essentially the same thing.\n\nAlso, converting clients to the new const-path api will require a transition period where we support both a builder and mutable paths.  Using `SkPathBuilder` for the migration seems like a good way to move things forward, even if in the end we replace its implementation with something else.",
